;; #1069 (RQ-60-VFPPRESSURE increment 2) — VFP pressure from HOMED LOCALS,
;; not operand-stack depth. jess's falcon measurement (fixture credit: jess):
;;
;;     LOCALS (homed)             OPERAND STACK (#881-rescued)
;;       13 locals : ok             30 deep : ok
;;       14 locals : EXHAUSTED      60 deep : ok
;;
;; Sixty simultaneously-live f32 on the operand stack compile (the #881 spill
;; rung rescues them); fourteen in homed locals do not — a home S-register is
;; pinned for the function's extent and the #881 victim search explicitly
;; skips homes. So the 13->14 wall is HOME residence, not register-file
;; capacity, and extending the pool into callee-saved S16..S31 would only
;; move the same wall outward.
;;
;;  * live13  — jess's NEGATIVE CONTROL: must keep compiling (base path,
;;              byte-identical by construction — the rung never fires).
;;  * live14  — the red line: param home S0 + 14 pinned local homes + tree
;;              temps > 16 S-registers. Fails on cortex-m7dp before the fix.
;;  * live16  — same wall, further in (jess measured 16 exhausted too).
;;  * live24  — 24 homed locals: forces MORE frame-resident locals than the
;;              default 8-slot spill pool holds, so the fix's slot demand
;;              composes with the #587 pool-grow retry INSIDE the VFP rung
;;              (this is the test that the reworded slot-exhaustion message
;;              still triggers the grow — the substring IS control flow).
;;  * live8d  — the f64 twin on m7dp: param home D0 + 8 pinned D homes
;;              exhausts the caller-saved D0..D7 pair file.
;;
;;  * wide60  — 60 homed locals consumed RIGHT-leaning, so every local stays
;;              live at once: beyond stage 2's reach (the 1020-byte VSTR/VLDR
;;              window), it compiles ONLY through the vfp-wide-file rung plus
;;              its pool-grow retry (#1439). The product saturates, so it can
;;              only see a SIGN error;
;;  * wsum60  — the same 60 locals summed right-leaning: the sum does not
;;              saturate, so it sees ANY wrong-register value. The wide file
;;              once handed out S16..S31 as aliases of S0..S15 (#1439); this
;;              export failed 9 of 14 rows on that binary, positives included.
;;
;; Every local is derived from the param (nothing constant-folds) and all are
;; consumed in ONE product tree, mirroring the falcon control-math shape
;; (attitude@0.7.0#tick / ekf@0.7.0#estimate, both phase-1 S exhaustion).
;;
